                      Stock Market For BBBBS

              This game was originally written by Ken Koch

           and was re-written to work on BBBBS by Matt English
                        2-29-92 (Leap year!)


   To set this game up, put "Stock_Market.rexx" into your Rexxdoors
   Directory. Then put "SM.companystats", "SM.help", and "smvars"
   in your Rexxdoors/Data Directory. After someone plays, more files
   will be generated in you rexxdoors/data directory.

   There are sysop functions available from inside the game. If your
   name is in the s:BBS.config file as the SYSOP, the game will show
   you the SYSOP MENU when you hit "Z" at the main menu.
   DON'T TRY TO RESET THE GAME UNTIL SOMEONE HAS PLAYED IT! The files
   involved in a reset, don't exist until someone has played!

   The original readme file follows this and it and the help file
   contain all the other info you'll need to play this game!

   The game will recognize what the players color preferences are set
   for in his user file and will respond accordingly.
   THANKS to Richard Lee Stocton for making the great BBBBS program,
   and for writing the color control routine that I used in this game!

